WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.120
RETO MEIER: Today, we're talking
about Google Workspace, Cloud

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.250
Functions, and the
Google Maps Platform.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.470
I'm Reto Meier, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud,"

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.240
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.670
news from the safety of home.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.010
Introducing Google
Workspace, everything

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.010
you need to get anything
done now in one place.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.470
Google Workspace includes
all of our productivity apps,

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.430
like Gmail, Calendar, and Drive,
now with three main upgrades.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.430
First, a new, deeply
integrated user experience

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.070
that helps teams collaborate
more effectively.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.960
Second, a new
brand identity that

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.780
reflects the way our
products works together.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.880
And third, new
ways to get started

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.680
with solutions and
price points tailored

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.220
to the unique needs of our
broad range of customers.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.470
Cloud Functions
recently leveled up,

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.570
now supporting new
run-times, new regions,

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.030
and fine grained
security controls.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.370
There's also new support
for local development

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.010
with the functions
framework, an upgraded code

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.170
editor in the cloud
console, and more ways

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.150
to control your costs.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.560
It's a long list of new
features and services.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.910
So be sure to check out the
blog post for a full recap.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.650
2020 has certainly been a
year of unexpected challenges,

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.690
and the upcoming
holiday shopping season

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.910
will likely see a few more.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.730
With the increased focus on
contactless shopping and order

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.590
pickup, it's a
good time to focus

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.140
on the omnichannel
shopping experience.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.700
To help, the Google
Maps platform

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.570
has two retail solutions, Store
Locator Plus and Checkout,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.330
and this blog covers how you
can leverage these services

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.010
to drive conversions.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.050
Season three of
"Seasons of Scale"

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.030
kicked off with Carter
Morgan explaining

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.550
how to break apps into
independent services

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.170
and aim for a stateless
cloud solution.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.630
So be sure to
check out the video

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:42.120
to follow along as
[? Criter ?] Junction choose

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.960
which monolithic apps should be
refactored into microservices,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.900
and how stateless
services made that easier.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.150
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.280
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.220
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.870
We'll see you in the cloud.

